Modifications by davidho27941 (2026-10-04):
- hooks/blast-radius.mjs: user-facing strings (pane labels, buttons, toast,
  measurement summaries and notes, refusal messages) now come from
  hooks/i18n.mjs through t(lang, key); a "session.start" hook reads LC_ALL,
  LC_MESSAGES and LANG to pick the language when the option is "auto";
  register(on, options) reads the "language" option; classify() is exported
  for the tests. Classification, measuring and holding logic are unchanged.
  The file keeps its original copyright header and carries a "Modified by"
  note beneath it.
- hooks/i18n.mjs (new): the strings in English, Traditional Chinese and
  Japanese, and resolveLang().
- .claude-plugin/plugin.json: gained a "userConfig" block with the "language"
  option (auto / en / zh-TW / ja). Name, version, description, author and
  keywords are the upstream's.
- tests/blast-radius.test.ts (new): tests for resolveLang, dictionary
  completeness and classify.
- README.md (new, English), NOTICE (this file), LICENSE (a copy of the
  upstream license) and tsconfig.json (editor type-checking against the types
  Claude Code lays in .claude-plugin/types/) were added by davidho27941.

Modifications by davidho27941 (2026-10-05):
- hooks/blast-radius.mjs: draw()'s first parameter was renamed from `t` to
  `ui`. Since the 2026-10-04 change it shadowed the imported translation
  function t(), so every pane rendered empty and every hold ended in the
  error refusal. No other change.
- tests/hold.test.tsx (new): tests of the hold itself (pane and band drawing,
  Cancel refuses, Proceed runs, language of the pane).

Unmodified upstream files: hooks/hooks.json, screenshots/*, and the upstream
README kept as README.upstream.md.
